(5040141, 733480, 62357, '<td valign="top">one of my faves.</td>', 'one of my faves.', '2008-11-03 00:58:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040144, 733486, 48560, '<td valign="top">gratz Judi! :)</td>', 'gratz Judi! :)', '2008-11-03 01:01:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040145, 733508, 97270, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LadyTara:</b></div><hr/><i> The title of this photo really touched me, it seemed so sad and the pic is very poignant with that title. I gave it an 8, had the petal not been in the way it''d have been more. I think this should''ve ranked higher than it has. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for the encouragement, Laura!</td>', 'Originally posted by LadyTara: The title of this photo really touched me, it seemed so sad and the pic is very poignant with that title. I gave it an 8, had the petal not been in the way it''d have been more. I think this should''ve ranked higher than it has.   Thank you for the encouragement, Laura!', '2008-11-03 01:01:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040148, 733714, 97225, '<td valign="top">This shot deserved a higher score than it got.(I gave you a 9 )</td>', 'This shot deserved a higher score than it got.(I gave you a 9 )', '2008-11-03 01:03:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040152, 733823, 72670, '<td valign="top">Brad, thought this would fare much better. Maybe its the models.</td>', 'Brad, thought this would fare much better. Maybe its the models.', '2008-11-03 01:04:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040173, 733549, 97225, '<td valign="top">Well I may as well confess that the child had not fallen off his bike. Some of you were onto me. However it was not posed either. My grandson can ride his bike a lot faster than I can walk! When he reaches a place that he must stop and wait (e.g. an intersection) he takes the opportunity to have a little rest until his slow grandparents catch up. I just thought that it looked like he had taken a spill.</td>', 'Well I may as well confess that the child had not fallen off his bike. Some of you were onto me. However it was not posed either. My grandson can ride his bike a lot faster than I can walk! When he reaches a place that he must stop and wait (e.g. an intersection) he takes the opportunity to have a little rest until his slow grandparents catch up. I just thought that it looked like he had taken a spill.', '2008-11-03 01:17:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040181, 732863, 68504, '<td valign="top">Ah.  I figured this for a blue.  Congratulations to both you and Don.</td>', 'Ah.  I figured this for a blue.  Congratulations to both you and Don.', '2008-11-03 01:24:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040185, 733465, 73452, '<td valign="top">COLEYYYY!!! YEA! always rooting for you man, its great to see your work ehre again!  Your wife is so sweet, lol, i wish i could have seen here there in real time!  great job once again, keep it up!</td>', 'COLEYYYY!!! YEA! always rooting for you man, its great to see your work ehre again!  Your wife is so sweet, lol, i wish i could have seen here there in real time!  great job once again, keep it up!', '2008-11-03 01:27:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040191, 733486, 48228, '<td valign="top">Awesome image here Judi, perfecty for the challenge, and so pleased you got a ribbon.....</td>', 'Awesome image here Judi, perfecty for the challenge, and so pleased you got a ribbon.....', '2008-11-03 01:36:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040193, 733798, 63806, '<td valign="top">Great Work!</td>', 'Great Work!', '2008-11-03 01:38:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040194, 733617, 66384, '<td valign="top">I love this shot. It has to be Germany, judging by the look on the woman''s face -- such disapproval. I really like the range you got in this shot, with the tourist in the back. I like the texture of the pavement, and I like the median (or round-about) with the lines of the pavers radiating out. <br/> <br/>It''s funny that the man is walking behind the woman even though they seem to be together. My husband does that to me all the time, and it really annoys me. I have to keep turning around if I want to speak to him, and to see if he is still there.</td>', 'I love this shot. It has to be Germany, judging by the look on the woman''s face -- such disapproval. I really like the range you got in this shot, with the tourist in the back. I like the texture of the pavement, and I like the median (or round-about) with the lines of the pavers radiating out.  It''s funny that the man is walking behind the woman even though they seem to be together. My husband does that to me all the time, and it really annoys me. I have to keep turning around if I want to speak to him, and to see if he is still there.', '2008-11-03 01:38:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040198, 733617, 68504, '<td valign="top">I too like the oddness and that great expanse of cobble, and Mrs. HappyFace.</td>', 'I too like the oddness and that great expanse of cobble, and Mrs. HappyFace.', '2008-11-03 01:41:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040204, 733486, 68514, '<td valign="top">I love street basketball, i love street photography, i love this shot, the BW conversion, lights and composiyion. Congrats for red ribbon Judi. Ciao, Paolo :)</td>', 'I love street basketball, i love street photography, i love this shot, the BW conversion, lights and composiyion. Congrats for red ribbon Judi. Ciao, Paolo :)', '2008-11-03 01:45:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040206, 733801, 68514, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot. Good perspective and PP. Congrats on this yellow. Ciao :)</td>', 'Very nice shot. Good perspective and PP. Congrats on this yellow. Ciao :)', '2008-11-03 01:46:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040225, 733661, 68504, '<td valign="top">Voted but didn''t comment. Beautiful use of your new lens! Congenial tones for all the elements.  Congenial feelings.</td>', 'Voted but didn''t comment. Beautiful use of your new lens! Congenial tones for all the elements.  Congenial feelings.', '2008-11-03 01:55:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5040229, 733381, 30214, '<td valign="top">great shot, real street photography at its best! well deserved blue.</td>', 'great shot, real street photography at its best! well deserved blue.', '2008-11-03 01:56:30.000000', NULL, 0),
