(5042596, 733438, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very cool shot Julianne. I love it. Congrats on the great score.</td>', 'Very cool shot Julianne. I love it. Congrats on the great score.', '2008-11-03 22:32:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042709, 733528, 62318, '<td valign="top">What I did not notice in the challenge are the two figures. One on the left and one on the right, seemingly moving around the fountain. It''s like a future merry-go-round that is implied. What, at least that is what I see...</td>', 'What I did not notice in the challenge are the two figures. One on the left and one on the right, seemingly moving around the fountain. It''s like a future merry-go-round that is implied. What, at least that is what I see...', '2008-11-03 23:48:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042725, 733438, 23098, '<td valign="top">Yes, mysterious. The smudges on the window and the grain all work well together in the b&amp;w conversion for a memorable photo.  This was one of my favorites in the challenge, Julianne.  I feel it should have done better. Nicely seen and photographed. It rocks. )</td>', 'Yes, mysterious. The smudges on the window and the grain all work well together in the b&w conversion for a memorable photo.  This was one of my favorites in the challenge, Julianne.  I feel it should have done better. Nicely seen and photographed. It rocks. )', '2008-11-04 00:07:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042727, 733062, 66384, '<td valign="top">It''s interesting that I feel there is more human interaction in this shot than in your outtake. There are as many people in the outtake, but I think the cars distract from them. <br/> <br/>As with the other shot, I really like the color in this shot, especially the reflected color on the pavement. And while I usually don''t like all the electrical equipment in a photo, you have so much of it here that it becomes an interesting feature -- the overhead traffic lights and the row of arched street lamps. The more I look at the shot, the more I find to like about it.</td>', 'It''s interesting that I feel there is more human interaction in this shot than in your outtake. There are as many people in the outtake, but I think the cars distract from them.  As with the other shot, I really like the color in this shot, especially the reflected color on the pavement. And while I usually don''t like all the electrical equipment in a photo, you have so much of it here that it becomes an interesting feature -- the overhead traffic lights and the row of arched street lamps. The more I look at the shot, the more I find to like about it.', '2008-11-04 00:11:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042735, 733824, 62318, '<td valign="top">I really like the geometry and the low perspective. It really fills in the frame nicely and the toning is wonderful. At first I thought it might be better if there was more interaction with the subject and the viewer, but the more I look at it the more I like how is just perfectly perpendicular. She is the scene.</td>', 'I really like the geometry and the low perspective. It really fills in the frame nicely and the toning is wonderful. At first I thought it might be better if there was more interaction with the subject and the viewer, but the more I look at it the more I like how is just perfectly perpendicular. She is the scene.', '2008-11-04 00:29:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042736, 733897, 62318, '<td valign="top">Jeb, beyond the choice in color, I think this is a well done photo. I really like the different areas of light and shadow you have going on in the shot.</td>', 'Jeb, beyond the choice in color, I think this is a well done photo. I really like the different areas of light and shadow you have going on in the shot.', '2008-11-04 00:31:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042738, 733528, 66384, '<td valign="top">From the standpoint of Street Photography, the person on the left gives the image action and humanity, however outside the confines of the challenge topic, I would prefer the composition without the figure. I like the large oval of the fountain filling the width of the frame, and I like the repeating yellows of the lights, building, tree, and fallen leaves. The dull light gives it an interesting atmosphere.</td>', 'From the standpoint of Street Photography, the person on the left gives the image action and humanity, however outside the confines of the challenge topic, I would prefer the composition without the figure. I like the large oval of the fountain filling the width of the frame, and I like the repeating yellows of the lights, building, tree, and fallen leaves. The dull light gives it an interesting atmosphere.', '2008-11-04 00:32:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042739, 733803, 62318, '<td valign="top">What works here is the natural tendency of grouping. I really like the interaction, there almost seems to be a reflection between the two groups. Colors are lovely too.</td>', 'What works here is the natural tendency of grouping. I really like the interaction, there almost seems to be a reflection between the two groups. Colors are lovely too.', '2008-11-04 00:33:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042740, 733674, 62318, '<td valign="top">Nice limited depth you used here Kashi. I get this nice somber feeling to the photo. Kind of hard to relate it to the challenge, perhaps a bit of street curb to the right would have really nailed it. Still the toning and the textures are superb.</td>', 'Nice limited depth you used here Kashi. I get this nice somber feeling to the photo. Kind of hard to relate it to the challenge, perhaps a bit of street curb to the right would have really nailed it. Still the toning and the textures are superb.', '2008-11-04 00:35:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042741, 733715, 66384, '<td valign="top">I like the action and the rain. And I like the b&amp;w conversion and contrast. I really feel for her. I think in her situation I would have headed for that open door.</td>', 'I like the action and the rain. And I like the b&w conversion and contrast. I really feel for her. I think in her situation I would have headed for that open door.', '2008-11-04 00:36:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042742, 733705, 62318, '<td valign="top">The limited depth and the hair flowing really nailed the one girl. Really, a terrific moment in capture your subject.</td>', 'The limited depth and the hair flowing really nailed the one girl. Really, a terrific moment in capture your subject.', '2008-11-04 00:36:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042743, 733547, 62318, '<td valign="top">I really like the double take here, with the reflection and the rider. Though not the same person, it does engage you in the photo.</td>', 'I really like the double take here, with the reflection and the rider. Though not the same person, it does engage you in the photo.', '2008-11-04 00:38:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042745, 733391, 62318, '<td valign="top">A very nice PJ piece. The lines and the jumbled mess really work well here.</td>', 'A very nice PJ piece. The lines and the jumbled mess really work well here.', '2008-11-04 00:39:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042746, 733486, 28359, '<td valign="top">Great capture, Congrats!!!</td>', 'Great capture, Congrats!!!', '2008-11-04 00:40:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042747, 733761, 62318, '<td valign="top">There are some really great things going on this picture. The perfect 3 on 3 (well 4 if you count the one person you can''t see), as well as the walk sign and the round shapes.</td>', 'There are some really great things going on this picture. The perfect 3 on 3 (well 4 if you count the one person you can''t see), as well as the walk sign and the round shapes.', '2008-11-04 00:41:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042754, 733715, 62318, '<td valign="top">It''s  a modern take on Cartier-Bresson''s shot of his friend Alberto Giacometti in the rain.<br/>Good stuff.</td>', 'It''s  a modern take on Cartier-Bresson''s shot of his friend Alberto Giacometti in the rain.Good stuff.', '2008-11-04 00:55:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042755, 733530, 66384, '<td valign="top">How interesting! I really like this. I really like the way you have created the border to continue the black in the image and to balance the composition. I like the bold colors and the geometry. And I really like the light. The composition is outstanding. I like the perspective of the huge shark and large person in the foreground with the small ship and very small person in the background. Marvelous image.</td>', 'How interesting! I really like this. I really like the way you have created the border to continue the black in the image and to balance the composition. I like the bold colors and the geometry. And I really like the light. The composition is outstanding. I like the perspective of the huge shark and large person in the foreground with the small ship and very small person in the background. Marvelous image.', '2008-11-04 00:55:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042757, 733486, 69668, '<td valign="top">This is a great shot.  Congrats on the red!!!</td>', 'This is a great shot.  Congrats on the red!!!', '2008-11-04 00:57:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042804, 733561, 41746, '<td valign="top">Brilliant shot. Underrated IMO.</td>', 'Brilliant shot. Underrated IMO.', '2008-11-04 03:00:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042901, 733486, 35708, '<td valign="top">Yes, congrats on the ribbon. This is a beautiful shot. I love the feeling of depth and just the overall "crispness'' of this photo.</td>', 'Yes, congrats on the ribbon. This is a beautiful shot. I love the feeling of depth and just the overall "crispness'' of this photo.', '2008-11-04 07:12:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042945, 733330, 68980, '<td valign="top">fab. the blur is yummy.</td>', 'fab. the blur is yummy.', '2008-11-04 08:33:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5042971, 733547, 66384, '<td valign="top">Such good processing. I''m so glad you posted the steps. Before I read them I was particularly taken with the subdued color, and was trying to understand what made it so special. I like the reflection in the window, and I get a really nice feeling from this little snip of the neighborhood -- the cobblestone streets and walk, the open door of the restaurant and the sun on the building across the street.</td>', 'Such good processing. I''m so glad you posted the steps. Before I read them I was particularly taken with the subdued color, and was trying to understand what made it so special. I like the reflection in the window, and I get a really nice feeling from this little snip of the neighborhood -- the cobblestone streets and walk, the open door of the restaurant and the sun on the building across the street.', '2008-11-04 09:00:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043083, 733761, 66384, '<td valign="top">This seems to be well processed for photojournalism, a nice clear shot of the moment, but I think for Street Photography (an art form) more contrast is needed. What I particularly like about this is the walk sign. The posture of the little walking man on the sign is echoed by all the pedestrians.</td>', 'This seems to be well processed for photojournalism, a nice clear shot of the moment, but I think for Street Photography (an art form) more contrast is needed. What I particularly like about this is the walk sign. The posture of the little walking man on the sign is echoed by all the pedestrians.', '2008-11-04 10:04:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043106, 733094, 66384, '<td valign="top">The people with the 3-D glasses really seem to be enjoying the experience. I like the light on their faces and the contrast in the image. I get a good feeling for the event, with some people milling around and visiting, and others still involved with the art.</td>', 'The people with the 3-D glasses really seem to be enjoying the experience. I like the light on their faces and the contrast in the image. I get a good feeling for the event, with some people milling around and visiting, and others still involved with the art.', '2008-11-04 10:23:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043115, 733756, 72136, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your comments, they really help a lot!<br/> <br/>@choltmeiher and Melethia: I only had time for this shot because the traffic started moving the second I shot this. My boyfriend was a couple of meters behind me and he had a different angle but I like his better :)<br/> <br/>@crabappl3: yes, you are right. it looked a lot lighter on my notebook when I was working on it. Now at my office it does look much darker :(<br/></td>', 'Thank you all for your comments, they really help a lot! @choltmeiher and Melethia: I only had time for this shot because the traffic started moving the second I shot this. My boyfriend was a couple of meters behind me and he had a different angle but I like his better :) @crabappl3: yes, you are right. it looked a lot lighter on my notebook when I was working on it. Now at my office it does look much darker :(', '2008-11-04 10:27:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043120, 733561, 24454, '<td valign="top">Oooh, I loved this one in the challenge and am so glad it did so well!  Street Photography at its best and most real!  Congratulations on such a deservingly high finish :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Oooh, I loved this one in the challenge and am so glad it did so well!  Street Photography at its best and most real!  Congratulations on such a deservingly high finish :) ', '2008-11-04 10:30:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043121, 733391, 66384, '<td valign="top">I smiled instantly when this image opened. It seems to be quite windy, and I have to think that selling balloons on a windy day must be quite difficult. It''s also a little sad to see him standing there with so many balloons, and nobody seems to be interested in buying one. That''s a valid message in itself, but I would really love to have seen a delighted child looking at the balloons.</td>', 'I smiled instantly when this image opened. It seems to be quite windy, and I have to think that selling balloons on a windy day must be quite difficult. It''s also a little sad to see him standing there with so many balloons, and nobody seems to be interested in buying one. That''s a valid message in itself, but I would really love to have seen a delighted child looking at the balloons.', '2008-11-04 10:33:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043295, 733402, 7473, '<td valign="top">Unfortunately I think you are right that a black and white photo probably would not have done as well....  This is a very timely capture and is defintly some good street photography.</td>', 'Unfortunately I think you are right that a black and white photo probably would not have done as well....  This is a very timely capture and is defintly some good street photography.', '2008-11-04 12:41:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043324, 733902, 30982, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, Tim - I thought this was delightful, and definitely meets the challenge!</td>', 'Nice shot, Tim - I thought this was delightful, and definitely meets the challenge!', '2008-11-04 12:51:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043328, 733486, 80096, '<td valign="top">Congrats! Wonderful shot!</td>', 'Congrats! Wonderful shot!', '2008-11-04 12:53:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043343, 733801, 80096, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your ribbon. Beautiful portrayal. Well deserved.</td>', 'Congrats on your ribbon. Beautiful portrayal. Well deserved.', '2008-11-04 12:57:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043346, 733381, 80096, '<td valign="top">Beautiful commentary piece. Very well done. Congrats on your first place win!</td>', 'Beautiful commentary piece. Very well done. Congrats on your first place win!', '2008-11-04 12:58:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043411, 733617, 65319, '<td valign="top">Oh that lady''s face with her husband in tow...clearly, a marriage made in Heaven...haha!  With the oblivious tourist in the background taking a photo...the door?!, this photo has street style and above all...CHARACTER!!!</td>', 'Oh that lady''s face with her husband in tow...clearly, a marriage made in Heaven...haha!  With the oblivious tourist in the background taking a photo...the door?!, this photo has street style and above all...CHARACTER!!!', '2008-11-04 13:26:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043414, 733636, 65319, '<td valign="top">Oh Sue!!!  Congrats on Top 10 (should have been in the Top 3 though)!!!  This photo carries the hallmark of your style...INTENSITY.  <br/></td>', 'Oh Sue!!!  Congrats on Top 10 (should have been in the Top 3 though)!!!  This photo carries the hallmark of your style...INTENSITY.  ', '2008-11-04 13:29:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043429, 733636, 30214, '<td valign="top">Great shot! However I would love it even more if it was not so over-processed - it does look kinda like a poster...</td>', 'Great shot! However I would love it even more if it was not so over-processed - it does look kinda like a poster...', '2008-11-04 13:38:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043437, 733631, 30214, '<td valign="top">nice understated image here. We don''t see the face, but the pose speaks for itself</td>', 'nice understated image here. We don''t see the face, but the pose speaks for itself', '2008-11-04 13:41:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043648, 733402, 82032, '<td valign="top">very cool shot.</td>', 'very cool shot.', '2008-11-04 16:16:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043793, 733351, 21124, '<td valign="top">I prefer this one to your other shot of the same place:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=732791" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/936/120/732791.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/936/120/732791.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/936/120/732791.jpg"/></a> <br/>Being closer to the painting reproduction provides more details to look at.</td>', 'I prefer this one to your other shot of the same place: Being closer to the painting reproduction provides more details to look at.', '2008-11-04 17:12:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043965, 733705, 66384, '<td valign="top">I like the focus on the girl with the blowing hair; she definitely has the energy in this image. The contrast and b&amp;w conversion are very effective. I''m not sure why you went with blue, and although I don''t mind it, I don''t see that it adds anything.</td>', 'I like the focus on the girl with the blowing hair; she definitely has the energy in this image. The contrast and b&w conversion are very effective. I''m not sure why you went with blue, and although I don''t mind it, I don''t see that it adds anything.', '2008-11-04 18:46:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043979, 733824, 66384, '<td valign="top">This is such an ironic shot. The location is so isolated, and the unhealthy looking woman standing under the vitamin sign holding high fat food is just so odd. I like the flat sky and the harsh light too. It all adds to the weirdness. Why is she just standing there like that? What is she waiting for? What is she looking at?</td>', 'This is such an ironic shot. The location is so isolated, and the unhealthy looking woman standing under the vitamin sign holding high fat food is just so odd. I like the flat sky and the harsh light too. It all adds to the weirdness. Why is she just standing there like that? What is she waiting for? What is she looking at?', '2008-11-04 18:54:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043983, 733897, 66384, '<td valign="top">I really like the composition and the yellow duotone. And the clarity/focus is lovely. Nothing seems to be going on here, so it seems more like a landscape than street photography. Still it is a very nice image.</td>', 'I really like the composition and the yellow duotone. And the clarity/focus is lovely. Nothing seems to be going on here, so it seems more like a landscape than street photography. Still it is a very nice image.', '2008-11-04 18:58:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5043997, 733803, 66384, '<td valign="top">There are a lot of things I like about this image. First of all, I love the colors of the boys jackets echoing the colors in the trees. Second, I like the grouping of the boys v.s. the men. And third I like the happy interaction between the members of each group. The whole image: colors, sunny day, social interaction, all add up to a very happy and cheerful scene. It makes me smile.</td>', 'There are a lot of things I like about this image. First of all, I love the colors of the boys jackets echoing the colors in the trees. Second, I like the grouping of the boys v.s. the men. And third I like the happy interaction between the members of each group. The whole image: colors, sunny day, social interaction, all add up to a very happy and cheerful scene. It makes me smile.', '2008-11-04 19:05:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5044004, 733674, 66384, '<td valign="top">Looks like a muddy yard rather than a street. Also there isn''t much going on. That makes it hard to connect this image with the challenge topic. However, I like the image -- the composition, the light, the texture, and the b&amp;w conversion.</td>', 'Looks like a muddy yard rather than a street. Also there isn''t much going on. That makes it hard to connect this image with the challenge topic. However, I like the image -- the composition, the light, the texture, and the b&w conversion.', '2008-11-04 19:11:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5044015, 733580, 66384, '<td valign="top">My first impression was, "whoa, too much noise reduction." But when I look at the camera exif data, I don''t understand why there would have been any noise. So I don''t understand why she looks so plastic. I think she is a very cute girl, and you captured a nice candid, but something didn''t work out in the processing.</td>', 'My first impression was, "whoa, too much noise reduction." But when I look at the camera exif data, I don''t understand why there would have been any noise. So I don''t understand why she looks so plastic. I think she is a very cute girl, and you captured a nice candid, but something didn''t work out in the processing.', '2008-11-04 19:20:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5044870, 732863, 53814, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the Blue, Joe. Great shot!</td>', 'Congratulations on the Blue, Joe. Great shot!', '2008-11-05 00:36:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5044991, 733636, 53814, '<td valign="top">Very interesting processing. This looks like the cover of a first edition from an alien teenagers comic book collection.<br/>Excellent.</td>', 'Very interesting processing. This looks like the cover of a first edition from an alien teenagers comic book collection.Excellent.', '2008-11-05 00:57:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5045014, 732863, 60915, '<td valign="top">Nice one dude! Bigfoot in the urban jungle! : )</td>', 'Nice one dude! Bigfoot in the urban jungle! : )', '2008-11-05 01:12:21.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5045483, 733381, 67319, '<td valign="top">Wow</td>', 'Wow', '2008-11-05 03:40:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5045580, 733381, 72102, '<td valign="top">very nice... it tells the whole story. congrates</td>', 'very nice... it tells the whole story. congrates', '2008-11-05 04:13:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5045600, 733524, 64670, '<td valign="top">WOW - my first thought was ''How did he get Megan Gale to pose for him'' ... and then I saw the whole picture - SO COOL!</td>', 'WOW - my first thought was ''How did he get Megan Gale to pose for him'' ... and then I saw the whole picture - SO COOL!', '2008-11-05 04:51:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5045886, 733715, 67258, '<td valign="top"><br/>Cheers from the Critique Club: <br/> <br/>Normally I would break down my critique to a review of the technicals, and then a more subjective peice on the impact the photo has on me.  This genre of photography, to me though, lends itself more to the latter response rather than looking at the technicals of how the end result was achieved.<br/> <br/>So, what works for me?  The viewpoint and composition give the viewer a feeling of being alone with just the subject, although seperated from them, both by virtue of having been taking from the comfort of the dry car, by the grainyness, and by the shield of the rain.  The rain is  as  important an element as the sodden running woman, and is very well portrayed.  The two lines on the pavement act as a  track, and increase the sense of her running through the downpour. <br/> <br/>What doesn''t work so well?  You stated that you are not happy with the composition, and it probably is the relative dullness of the background that contributes to the middle-of-the-pack score (combined, of course, with voters who want everything crystal sharp regardless of genre, intent etc...).  One of the comments below remarks on how the Open sign should somehow be more integral to the image, and I would have to agree.  As it is, it is just there, yes it draws your attention to the fact that despite available shelter she still chooses to run in the rain, and yes it provides juxtaposition of sorts, but it just doesn''t somehow come together in a completely succesfull way.<br/> <br/>I am not sure I have been particularly articulate here - at the end of the day it is a photo that I have enjoyed looking at in detail, but not one that engages me as fully as I wish it did.<br/> <br/>If you wish to raise any questions - or to disagree with me - do send me a PM.<br/> <br/>regards,<br/> <br/>Sara.<br/> <br/><i>Edit:  There was something about this photo that made me somewhat uncomfortable - I have just realised what it is.  The pose of the running woman is a side-on version of the same pose of the running girl fleeing from My Lai, right down to the position of her hand.  That I even made that connection makes me uncomfortable, because there is no sense in your photo of someone escaping from horrors unbearable.  Strange.</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-11-05 08:48:59.</i></td>', 'Cheers from the Critique Club:  Normally I would break down my critique to a review of the technicals, and then a more subjective peice on the impact the photo has on me.  This genre of photography, to me though, lends itself more to the latter response rather than looking at the technicals of how the end result was achieved. So, what works for me?  The viewpoint and composition give the viewer a feeling of being alone with just the subject, although seperated from them, both by virtue of having been taking from the comfort of the dry car, by the grainyness, and by the shield of the rain.  The rain is  as  important an element as the sodden running woman, and is very well portrayed.  The two lines on the pavement act as a  track, and increase the sense of her running through the downpour.  What doesn''t work so well?  You stated that you are not happy with the composition, and it probably is the relative dullness of the background that contributes to the middle-of-the-pack score (combined, of course, with voters who want everything crystal sharp regardless of genre, intent etc...).  One of the comments below remarks on how the Open sign should somehow be more integral to the image, and I would have to agree.  As it is, it is just there, yes it draws your attention to the fact that despite available shelter she still chooses to run in the rain, and yes it provides juxtaposition of sorts, but it just doesn''t somehow come together in a completely succesfull way. I am not sure I have been particularly articulate here - at the end of the day it is a photo that I have enjoyed looking at in detail, but not one that engages me as fully as I wish it did. If you wish to raise any questions - or to disagree with me - do send me a PM. regards, Sara. Edit:  There was something about this photo that made me somewhat uncomfortable - I have just realised what it is.  The pose of the running woman is a side-on version of the same pose of the running girl fleeing from My Lai, right down to the position of her hand.  That I even made that connection makes me uncomfortable, because there is no sense in your photo of someone escaping from horrors unbearable.  Strange.', '2008-11-05 08:42:49.000000', '2008-11-05 08:48:59.000000', 0),
(5046041, 733465, 11351, '<td valign="top">Excellent shot but better story :) Good job</td>', 'Excellent shot but better story :) Good job', '2008-11-05 10:06:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5046374, 733465, 68514, '<td valign="top">I think this is a cool idea very well executed. Maybe you didn''t ribbon because it doesn''t looks as candid as street phography needs, and it''s a pity. Anyway, Bravo :)</td>', 'I think this is a cool idea very well executed. Maybe you didn''t ribbon because it doesn''t looks as candid as street phography needs, and it''s a pity. Anyway, Bravo :)', '2008-11-05 12:18:50.000000', NULL, 0),
